From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:50:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: bound zero-timeout queue wait retries

A zero-timeout message poll can repeatedly observe a signaled server queue
while process_driver_events() reports no matching input. The absolute timeout
does not stop NtWaitForMultipleObjects from returning the signaled queue again,
so the poll spins until the queue changes. Return WAIT_TIMEOUT after processing
that stale wake once; real driver events still return through the existing path.
---
diff --git a/dlls/win32u/message.c b/dlls/win32u/message.c
--- a/dlls/win32u/message.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/message.c
@@ -3464,4 +3464,10 @@ static DWORD wait_message( DWORD count, const HANDLE *handles, DWORD timeout, DW
         if (probe) repeat_driver_ms += NtGetTickCount() - start;
         if (more) break;
+        /* A zero-timeout poll must not spin while the server queue stays signaled. */
+        if (!timeout)
+        {
+            ret = WAIT_TIMEOUT;
+            break;
+        }
     }
     while (ret == count - 1);
-- 
